name hobsub
category Package
revision 52810
shortdesc Construct package bundles
relocated 1
longdesc Heiko Oberdiek's hobsub package (and hobsub-hyperref and
longdesc hobsub-generic packages) defined a mechanism for concatenating
longdesc multiple files into a single file for faster loading. The
longdesc disadvantage is that it introduces hard dependencies between
longdesc the source files that are included and complicates distribution
longdesc and updates. It was principally used with hyperref but is not
longdesc currently used in any standard packages in TeX Live. The
longdesc packages are still distributed as simple stubs that reference
longdesc the included packages via \RequirePackage rather than copying
longdesc their source. The documented source of the original packages is
longdesc available at github, but is not distributed to CTAN.
runfiles size=3
 RELOC/tex/latex/hobsub/hobsub-generic.sty
 RELOC/tex/latex/hobsub/hobsub-hyperref.sty
 RELOC/tex/latex/hobsub/hobsub.sty
